    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d408">

                <pb facs="0834" n="800" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v15p1/pg800"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Matthews files, lot 53 D 413: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Joint Chiefs of Staff to the Commander in Chief
                        Far East (Clark)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top
                            secret<lb/>priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-02-27T15:54:00-05:00">February 27, 1953—3:54
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>JCS 932457. From JCS reur C 61283.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d408-f1"/></p>
                <pb facs="0835" n="801" xml:id="pg801"/>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Re part 1. Comment on statement withheld pending final dec to implement
                        course of action outlined in para 2 of JCS 931311.<anchor n="2"
                            xml:id="d408-f2"/></item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Re part 2. To facilitate diplomatic consultation State has queried JCS re
                        possibility obtaining pertinent oblique aerial photos of Kaesong area as
                        documentation for charges of Commie buildup. If you have available oblique
                        photos with appropriate interpretive notations indicating location of mil
                        facilities that would be useful this purpose, request they be provided
                        ASAP.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Re part 3. Statement approved subject to deletion first sentence para E
                        and words “tolerated this military buildup and” in second sentence of same
                        para.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d408-f1" n="1" xml:id="d408-f1-content">
                <p>In this telegram, Feb. 19, 1953, Clark concurred with the views of the JCS as set
                    forth in paragraph 2 of JCS 931311, Feb. 13, <ref target="#pg776">p. 776</ref>,
                    and included a proposed letter announcing to the Communists his intention to
                    remove the immunity of the Kaesong and Munsan-ni restricted areas, should that
                    decision be made in Washington. (Matthews files, lot 53 D 413)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d408-f2" n="2" xml:id="d408-f2-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d408-f1">footnote 1</ref>, above.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
